	spec: 'Hal keeps its plumbing visible: AGENTS.md and tasks/README.md require user-facing inspection of exact model tool arguments, execution controls and failures rather than hiding them behind friendly summaries. Expanded tool cards show every supplied argument in readable labelled text, preserving multiline commands and descriptions, lists and nested structures without JSON/ASON; unknown and invalid arguments remain visible. Bash details distinguish omitted declarations and default controls from supplied values, identify the tool and call, and retain access to full output. Closed cards remain concise. Bash modifies accepts relative paths/globs without parent traversal and absolute paths/globs beneath /tmp, since allowed scratch writes must be declarable; other absolute paths, NULs, empty paths and non-string entries remain rejected before launch. Absolute /tmp literals and globs participate in snapshots, sensitive-file checks and canonical overlap locks, and retain absolute names in file-change records. Errors identify the invalid modifies entry and reason, give allowed path forms and state that the command did not run. Tool schema and SYSTEM.md explain these forms. Behavioral tests exercise absolute scratch snapshots/glob creation and invalid declarations, and complete human-readable argument presentation.',
